# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file.
#
# Documented ignores for three Snyk Code (SAST) findings that are proven false
# positives. Each already has a real, verified code-level mitigation; Snyk's
# taint engine structurally cannot recognize the barrier (it would require
# either breaking functionality or removing an intentional feature). See the
# inline `deepcode ignore` comment at each site for the full rationale.
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  go/XSS:
    - internal/server/gh_markdown.go:
        reason: >-
          Rendered markdown is allowlist-sanitized by bluemonday
          (markdownSanitizer), which strips javascript:/data: URLs, inline event
          handlers, and disallowed elements — the same approach GitHub uses.
          Snyk's go/XSS only credits stdlib HTML-escaping, which would defeat
          markdown rendering. Verified by TestMarkdownSanitizesDangerousSchemes.
        expires: 2027-08-04T00:00:00.000Z
  go/Ssrf:
    - internal/emojigen/main.go:
        reason: >-
          Build-time asset-vendoring tool. The request target is a compile-time
          constant (twemojiTarballURL), validated https/host by
          ensureTwemojiURLIsPinnedHTTPS and SHA-256 pinned after fetch; it is
          never derived from caller input, an environment value, or a redirect.
        expires: 2027-08-04T00:00:00.000Z
  go/TooPermissiveTrustManager:
    - internal/server/webhooks.go:
        reason: >-
          InsecureSkipVerify IS the opt-in webhook insecure_ssl=1 feature
          (GitHub exposes the same switch) and cannot exist without relaxing
          chain/hostname verification. The VerifyConnection callback still
          rejects absent or expired certificates and TLS is floored at 1.2, so
          the client is not a blanket accept-anything trust manager.
        expires: 2027-08-04T00:00:00.000Z
